.page env 1 run a program in a modified environment

# SYNOPSIS
*env* [*-i*] [_NAME_=_VALUE_]... [_COMMAND_ [_ARGUMENT_...]]

# DESCRIPTION
Without a _COMMAND_, `env` prints the environment, one `NAME=VALUE` per line. With one, it runs it after applying the assignments, searching the directories of `PATH`.

# OPTIONS
@ *-i*
    Start from an empty environment instead of the current one.

# EXIT STATUS
The command's own, or 127 if it was not found, 126 if it could not be run.

# EXAMPLES
    env
    env EDITOR=cat pnote
    env -i /bin/printenv

# SEE ALSO
printenv(1), gapsh(1)
